me":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T08:22:22-07:00","id":160850,"title":"","content":"That's not true. Sometimes we bitch about Pittsburgh and Baltimore too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/36-tomewilson","name":"tomewilson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar36_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T23:25:56-07:00","id":161446,"title":"","content":"And hating on New York, don't forget hating New York.<br /> <br /> And Ben Franklin. Sweet Jesus, Ben Franklin.<br /> <br /> Also, Leaper, if you're gonna write down the city at least use the proper grammar and spelling. It's a major city and you're dealing with people from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T23:39:07-07:00","id":161452,"title":"","content":"There's also a strong culture of loyalty and love of sports teams. I was once told a riot in Philly after a major win was &quot;drunken revelry&quot;, from the mouth of a native Philadelphian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T23:52:22-07:00","id":161456,"title":"","content":"Are Philadelphians particularly proud of Ben Franklin?<br /> <br /> I'll admit the extent of my time in Philly was passing through, going to Geno's Steaks and being a bit put off by all the bald eagles and all caps &quot;WE ONLY ACCEPT ORDERS IN ENGLISH&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> Do you guys as native Philadelphians think that the World of Darkness version of the city overplays the loyalty to neighborhoods? In the neighborhoods you're from, do you know a lot of the people in your neighborhoods? Or is life there more anonymous?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T06:51:32-07:00","id":161650,"title":"","content":"Ben Franklin is the patron saint of Philadelphia. Can't take two steps without seeing him on a poster, an ad, or in giant statue form.<br /> <br /> Taking that as a cue, you could say that the city reflects his lifestyle and values. We're loyal to a fault, we're passionate and stubborn, we work extremely hard on the things that matter to us, and when we join a celebration, it turns into an epic event. Think of the worst New York neighborhood with all its crime blended perfectly with the best of Paris.<br /> <br /> As for the neighborhoods, they shift very slowly and are fairly homogenous, so it's an easy way to identify a stranger.<br /> <br /> One other thing of note is, we're connected to Camden, New Jersey by the Ben Franklin Bridge. In the early 1900s, Camden was an affluent city, but has since become one of the murder capitals of the USA. Long story short, the police had to abandon it for a few years, because they didn't have the budget to defend it. <br /> <br /> More crime = Less legitimate citizens living there = Less taxes = Less money for cops = More crime, etc.<br /> <br /> They very recently started taking it back, but they have to rely on military tech similar to what we use in Iraq and Afghanistan just to secure a foothold because it's so lawless.<br /> <br /> If I had to WoD the city, I'd say it's primarily Union, with some Ascending One and Net0 gangs making a buck, a pocket of AKD in the museum district, and a very strong group of affluent Ashwood Abbey.<br /> <br /> To the west of Philadelphia is God fearing people fit for The Long Night, and to the east of Philadelphia in Camden is prime vampire feeding ground with an opportunity to get away with TF:V style action directly in public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/36-tomewilson","name":"tomewilson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar36_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T07:16:18-07:00","id":161686,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://fc03.deviantart.net/fs70/i/2011/332/9/f/ben_franklin_vs__zeus_by_sharpwriter-d4hjp6a.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> As badass as this is, I'm still betting on Zeus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T07:43:07-07:00","id":161711,"title":"","content":"Ah, but no one believes in Zeus anymore. Also remember that there's the greater Philadelphia area, prime ground for tier one cells, Union, and Long Night, with a few Baes in the more affluent burbs. They're generally considered part of the area, but they're not quite as rough or loyal as the city raised guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T07:53:43-07:00","id":161716,"title":"","content":"You know what would be cool? If the two of you made a google map of Philly with pins on it to show exactly where each cell or monster is found. Not from the books; start from scratch.<br /> <br /> It probably wouldn't take that long; if you kept it to just the names of the cell and which org (if any) they belong too.<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW; Bryn Mawr College is just outside Philly - and it's one of the seven sisters collages so expect the Maidens Blood Sisterhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-07-2014, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T08:18:13-07:00","id":161725,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in doing that. Admittedly though I'm using factionalized locales. My first Hunter story I've been writing up takes place in a neighborhood called Summerville based on Strawberry Mansion, and in places in Center City as well.<br /> <br /> Where do you think the best places for feeding might be for the Vampires?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 06-07-2014, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T08:39:50-07:00","id":161754,"title":"","content":"Center City, all the college/hipster bars in that area are perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T16:09:05-07:00","id":162870,"title":"","content":"More information on how Camden is a lot like Robocop's version of Detroit &gt; <a href=\"http://www.rollingstone.com/culture/news/apocalypse-new-jersey-a-dispatch-from-americas-most-desperate-town-20131211\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.rollingstone.com/culture/...-town-20131211</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/36-tomewilson","name":"tomewilson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar36_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T16:09:48-07:00","id":162872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/155500-extra-philadelphia-material?p=161446#post161446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And hating on New York, don't forget hating New York.<br /> <br /> And Ben Franklin. Sweet Jesus, Ben Franklin.<br /> <br /> Also, Leaper, if you're gonna write down the city at least use the proper grammar and spelling. It's a major city and you're dealing with people from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>uhh no.<br /> <br /> the movie rocky was set in philidelphia and there's a statue of rocky is there. maybe that's important to philidelphia.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:15:17-07:00","id":163029,"title":"","content":"Rocky means something to the older Italians in the city who were old enough to see the movie in the theater, but that phenomenon has died down and the statue is now considered a tourist trap.<br /> <br /> But if anyone in power ever considered removing said statue, we'd burn the whole fucking place to the ground in protest. We're just sentimental like that I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/36-tomewilson","name":"tomewilson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar36_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}